repo: atongsa/luantidyssey
file: PACKAGING.log
purpose: how to test this game on your machine, how to zip it, and how publishing works

This is a log, not a design doc. The design is GAME_MODE.md. Read that first.
The name is luantidyssey. It is not a DotA game.
The playable slice is smaller than the poem: hall, gold, lotus task, four skills, one wave.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOCAL TEST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Install Luanti 5.6 or newer.
   https://www.luanti.org/

2. Get this repository onto the machine (git clone or a zip of the repo).

3. The game directory must contain game.conf directly inside it.
   The folder name Luanti uses is luantidyssey.
   If you still have an old folder named luanti_dotA, rename it or replace it.
   Old worlds made under the old name will not pick this up. Make a new world.

4. Copy that folder into the user games directory. Typical paths:
   Linux, older:        ~/.minetest/games/luantidyssey
   Linux, newer Luanti: ~/.local/share/luanti/games/luantidyssey
   Windows:             %APPDATA%\Luanti\games\luantidyssey
                        or %APPDATA%\Minetest\games\luantidyssey
   macOS:               ~/Library/Application Support/luanti/games/luantidyssey
                        or ~/Library/Application Support/minetest/games/luantidyssey
   If none of those exist: open Luanti, Credits tab, "Open user data directory",
   then put the folder in games/ inside that directory.

5. Start Luanti. Create a NEW world.
   Game: luantidyssey.
   Any world name. Leave the mapgen dropdown alone.
   This game switches mapgen to singlenode and builds its own pad.
   Do not open an old world from another game.

6. What you should see
   Missing textures are possible (purple/black). Point at a block: the name is the UI.
   F5 turns on the debug HUD if you need node names.
   F7 twice switches to third person. That is the normal Luanti key, not a special camera.

7. How to play the slice
   You stand near the Hall of Ithaca.
   A journal opens almost at once. Spend one skill point on one of the four skills.
   Punch a gold stone. +5 gold. It goes dull and comes back after a few seconds.
   Slot 1 is a sword. Slot 2 is the journal. Punch with the journal to open it again.
   About 12 seconds in: three suitors and one taller lead suitor walk the path.
   Suitors hurt you if they stand on you. The lead hits harder and has more life.
   Right-click the lotus stand and refuse it. That also gives experience.
   A normal suitor who reaches the hall takes 30 hall life. The lead takes 50.
   Hall starts at 100.
   Win: lotus refused, all four dead, hall above 0.
   Lose: hall reaches 0.
   Each level gives another skill point. Highest rank is 3.
   Chat command /ml prints gold, hall, task, and skill ranks.
   Chat command /ml_reset (needs the server privilege) puts the slice back to the start.

8. If the pad is missing or you fall forever
   Make a new world with game luantidyssey. Do not copy an old world.mt over it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SKILLS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Four skills. A point learns one or raises it, up to rank 3.
Names are original.

  armor   Bronze voice
  weapon  Brand
  fruit   Bitter fruit
  blood   Cut the vein

Open: punch the journal, or type /journal
Cast: the Cast button, or /skill armor   /skill weapon   /skill fruit   /skill blood

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZIP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The zip must have one top folder, and game.conf must be one level under it.

Correct:
  luantidyssey/game.conf
  luantidyssey/mods/ml_core/init.lua
  luantidyssey/PACKAGING.log

Wrong:
  game.conf sitting at the root of the zip
  a zip of the .git directory alone

From the parent of the repo folder:

  zip -r luantidyssey.zip luantidyssey -x '*.git*'

Test the zip by deleting the games/luantidyssey folder, unzipping this archive into games/,
and starting a new world as in LOCAL TEST.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLISH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The in-game browser is ContentDB: https://content.luanti.org/

ContentDB only accepts packages under a license the FSF and/or the OSI call free.
This game is MIT. See LICENSE. That grant is what makes a later publish possible.
The package has not been submitted. Publishing still needs your ContentDB account.

Until then, give people the git URL or the zip. They install it with LOCAL TEST.
Luanti has no official "export this game as its own .exe" button.
The engine is LGPLv2.1. This game is MIT. Those are different licenses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT IS NOT IN THIS SLICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No cyclops or later stops. No second player.
No locked camera. No strategy base. This is not a DotA game.
Greek models are not in yet. The pad is still flat color.
